    "acquired_at": "2026-11-12T14:06:40.885143+00:00",
    "available_at": "2026-11-12T14:06:40.885143+00:00",
    "body": "A new chemical plant opened this week at BASF’s manufacturing complex in Geismar, Louisiana, completing a roughly $1 billion expansion that began in 2018. The project nearly doubles the site’s capacity for methylene diphenyl diisocyanate, or MDI, to about 600,000 metric tons a year.\nWhat’s Related\nBASF confirmed that the new plant has started up. The company called the expansion its largest wholly owned investment in North America and said the added capacity makes it the region’s largest MDI producer.\n“With this expansion, BASF is taking the lead in MDI production in North America,” said Ramkumar Dhruva, president of BASF’s Monomers Division. The company did not say when it expects the site to reach its full annual capacity.\nThree-phase expansion\nBASF carried out the project in three phases at its existing Geismar complex in Ascension Parish. A new unit for making MDI began operating in October 2020. In 2021, BASF expanded several units that feed into MDI production, increasing the complex’s capacity by about a third.\nBASF broke ground on the final phase in January 2023 after announcing a $780 million investment in that portion of the project. The final phase added units for earlier steps in the manufacturing process, along with equipment that separates the chemical into different products. BASF said the new equipment gives the plant more flexibility to adjust production to customer needs.\nWhat is MDI?\nManufacturers use MDI to make polyurethane, a material found in building insulation and appliances. It’s also used in vehicles, furniture, and footwear. By expanding at Geismar, BASF can make more of the chemical closer to its North American customers while using the infrastructure and raw material supply already in place at the complex.\nThe project also expanded production capacity for aniline, a chemical used to make MDI. BASF said it can now sell aniline directly from Geismar to North American customers that make agricultural chemicals, rubber, dyes and pigments.",
    "body_sha256": "8773e39445c161bc40da9b08b360d79cf9f852565b39b7aea602adf4790f29af",
